2026-08-30T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Cluster TLS is decided before data, and certificates carry v3 extensions
 # uuid: 8184f705-0710-5de0-a4bc-1fdc5f843ce8
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-08-30T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2134) 'mutual TLS on the weftspun-fdb cluster, and the client identity a service presents
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2134) 'weftspun-fdb on Fly; spot-broker as the first client; any later FDB client
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Cluster TLS is decided before data, and every certificate carries v3 extensions.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The weftspun-fdb cluster came up plaintext, and its backup could not reach the blob store: FoundationDB uses one TLS policy for peers and for S3, so a cluster with no trust store cannot speak HTTPS to Tigris.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Check a new cluster or client certificate against the v3 profile before you push it. The sections below hold the profile and the procedure on a live plaintext cluster.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Cluster TLS is decided before data, and certificates carry v3 extensions
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Mutual TLS from a private CA, per-machine certificates named by Fly machine ID, and one client certificate per consuming service, all carrying X.509v3 extensions, because FoundationDB's preverification rejects a bare `openssl req -x509` CA as `invalid CA certificate`. The profile, the local Docker proof with its negative control, and the full procedure are in DETAILS.md.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2134) 'A client is a TLS peer like any other: it presents its own leaf (`CN=fdb-spot-broker.chibifire.com`) through the `FDB_TLS_*` env vars libfdb_c reads, and verifies the cluster with the same rule the cluster uses (`Check.Valid=1,S.CN>=fdb-,S.CN<=.chibifire.com`).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Verification
 # tags: rfd:section-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2134) 'A matched pair in local Docker before any push: v3 certificates form a database; the previous extension-less certificates reproduce the production failure on the same server and rule. In prod, a ledger event survived a full machine replacement and read back over TLS.
 # tags: rfd:section
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The known wall
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The known wall is recorded in datasource-store's fdb-entrypoint and held exactly: there is no in-place path from a plaintext cluster to a TLS one, because `:tls` is part of a coordinator's address and the coordinated state on disk names addresses that no longer exist. The gated `WEFT_FDB_RESET=1` wipe is the remedy, so TLS is decided before there is data worth keeping; this cluster held one test event.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The failure this profile exists for
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2134) 'With certificates from a bare `openssl req -x509` CA and extension-less `openssl x509 -req` leaves, every fdbserver logged, on each handshake:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2134) '    Type="TLSPolicyFailure" Reason="preverification failed"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2134) '    VerifyError="invalid CA certificate"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2134) 'and `status` reported the cluster's coordinators unreachable, the same line a network fault produces. Read the trace event, not the status line.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The profile
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The 10-year CA and 2-year leaf numbers below were retracted by RFD66606-2145 on 2026-09-01. The current guidance is 25-year `notAfter` on the offline root with 5-year policy rotation, 3-year intermediates, and 90-day service leaves; see RFD66606-2145 and its `references/` for the CFF citations. The lines are kept in place so a reader working from an older linked reference can see what the values used to say and what they moved to.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2134) 'CA (`fdb-ca.chibifire.com`, 4096-bit RSA, 10 years):
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2134) '    basicConstraints = critical, CA:true
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2134) '    keyUsage         = critical, keyCertSign, cRLSign
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2134) '    subjectKeyIdentifier = hash
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Leaf (2048-bit RSA, 2 years), one per machine and one per client service:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2134) '    basicConstraints = CA:false
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2134) '    keyUsage         = critical, digitalSignature, keyEncipherment
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2134) '    extendedKeyUsage = serverAuth, clientAuth
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2134) '    subjectKeyIdentifier   = hash
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2134) '    authorityKeyIdentifier = keyid, issuer
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Subjects: `fdb-<fly machine id>.chibifire.com` for cluster machines, `fdb-<service>.chibifire.com` for clients (`fdb-spot-broker.chibifire.com`). The machine ID survives `fly machine update`, which the entrypoint records a NIC-named scheme failing. All pass the one verify rule: `Check.Valid=1,S.CN>=fdb-,S.CN<=.chibifire.com`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The proof, run before the push
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2134) 'One `foundationdb/foundationdb:7.3.63` container, one fdbserver on `127.0.0.1:4500:tls`, the cluster's verify rule on both ends:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2134) '| certificates | result |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2134) '| --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2134) '| v3 profile above | handshake clean, `configure new single memory` creates the database, 0 TLSPolicyFailure |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2134) '| extension-less (what production had) | `The database is unavailable`: the production symptom, reproduced |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The negative control is the point: the same server, rule, and commands separate the two cert sets, so the diagnosis is the extensions and not the rule, the addresses, or Fly.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The procedure on a live plaintext cluster
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2134) '1. Certificates as above; base64 each PEM (`base64 -w0`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2134) '2. `fly secrets set` on weftspun-fdb: `FDB_TLS_CA_B64`, and per machine `FDB_TLS_CERT_<machine id>_B64` / `FDB_TLS_KEY_<machine id>_B64`. The entrypoint takes the pair addressed to the machine and refuses to borrow another's.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2134) '3. The cluster will NOT form: coordinated state on disk names the plaintext addresses. This is the entrypoint's documented wall. `fly secrets set WEFT_FDB_RESET=1` wipes the data directories on restart; the lowest address reconfigures the database.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2134) '4. Verify with a TLS-armed fdbcli (`--tls_certificate_file`, `--tls_key_file`, `--tls_ca_file`, `--tls_verify_peers`), then `fly secrets unset WEFT_FDB_RESET` and verify again; the second check proves a restart no longer wipes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2134) '5. Each client service: its own leaf via `FDB_TLS_CERT_B64` / `FDB_TLS_KEY_B64` / `FDB_TLS_CA_B64` secrets, materialised to files at start and handed to libfdb_c through `FDB_TLS_CERTIFICATE_FILE`, `FDB_TLS_KEY_FILE`, `FDB_TLS_CA_FILE`, `FDB_TLS_VERIFY_PEERS`; the cluster string gains `:tls` on every coordinator.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2134) 'What the prod verification measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2134) 'spot-broker's `POST /target/zero` wrote a ledger event through the iceoryx2 bus into the TLS cluster. The broker machine was then fully replaced by a deploy (no volume exists on that app), and `GET /status` on the new machine returned the same event. That is the durability the architecture claims, measured: the machine held nothing, and the data came back from the cluster.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The backup, measured locally and blocked on SNI in prod
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2134) 'With the CA present the trust bundle forms (151 anchors) and OpenSSL verifies Tigris against it, yet `fdbbackup` times out. The trace names it: `N2_ConnectHandshakeError ErrorMsg="stream truncated"` against both the A and the AAAA record. FoundationDB's blobstore client sends no SNI, and Tigris's edge requires it; curl succeeds from the same machine because curl sends it. The knob `resolve_prefer_ipv4_addr` changes which address dies, not whether.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The controlled counterpart ran in local Docker against [versitygw](https://github.com/versity/versitygw) (Apache-2.0), a server that presents its one certificate without SNI. Same fdbbackup, same CA profile, same verify-rule shape:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2134) '1. the TLS handshake completes, so the client's TLS is fine and SNI is the whole difference;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2134) '2. `--knob_http_request_aws_v4_header=true` is required, versitygw refuses FoundationDB's default SigV2 (Tigris also speaks v4);
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2134) '3. the bucket must pre-exist, FoundationDB's create-bucket body is refused as MalformedXML; created through the S3 API, the backup submits and runs: `The backup on tag 'default' is in progress`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The production hop that landed is stunnel, not the versitygw sidecar first named here: the job needed only SNI added to a TCP stream, and a second S3 implementation in the path was more moving parts than eleven lines of stunnel config. The operator rescinded versitygw on 2026-11-16, and SeaweedFS is the S3-compatible server (RFD66606-2364). One more wall surfaced live, Tigris routes buckets from the Host header, so the endpoint's name has to survive the hop (/etc/hosts points it at loopback after the IP is resolved for stunnel's literal dial). datasource-store PRs #4 and #5 carry the change; `logbook-rfd2134-backup-through-the-sni-hop.md` carries the measurements, ending with kvrange objects listed in the bucket.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2134) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-30T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2134) 'Turning TLS on after the fact hit two walls, one known and one new.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2134  1 LINE
 Text:Written

